# Base URL of the daily-puzzle backend (Lambda Function URL behind CloudFront, #2).
# The server is the authoritative time source and serves "today's" puzzle.
#
# For LOCAL DEV: copy this to `.env.local` (gitignored) and point it at your backend.
# Local backend harness (#17): run `pnpm backend:dev` and point this at it, then
# `pnpm dev` resolves today's puzzle end-to-end (publish a puzzle to the local store
# with `pnpm puzzle:publish` to test a specific one):
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787
#
# For a PRODUCTION BUILD (`pnpm build`): `.env.production` already holds the deployed
# backend URL (BackendStack `ApiUrl`, https://api.whippin.ai), but the build also REQUIRES
# a Turnstile site key. CI injects the real repo variable; a local build may copy this file
# to `.env.local` and use the test key below.
#
# Required for dev/build. The frontend must not silently use its own origin as the backend.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787

# Privacy-first analytics (Plausible, #60). The site's domain as registered in Plausible
# (e.g. whippin.ai). LEAVE THIS UNSET for dev/preview/local builds — analytics stays
# fully inert (no tracker loaded, every track() a no-op). It is set ONLY on the CI
# production deploy via a GitHub repo variable (see .github/workflows/deploy.yml) and is
# deliberately NOT committed to .env.production, so only the deployed site reports.
# (Contrast VITE_API_BASE_URL, which IS committed there: the app needs a backend on every
# build, but analytics must arm ONLY on the real CI-deployed site — never a local/preview
# build. Deploys go through CI, i.e. PR -> checks -> merge -> deploy, not local builds.)
# VITE_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=whippin.ai

# Cloudflare Turnstile SITE key (#170) — the public half of the pair whose SECRET the
# backend verifies via Siteverify (#169, SSM /whippin/turnstile-secret). Used to mint the
# invisible token a score submission carries; PUBLIC by nature (baked into the bundle),
# like every VITE_ var. Local DEV may leave it unset to disable submission silently; a
# production build refuses an unset value. The value below is Cloudflare's documented
# always-passing INVISIBLE TEST key — pair it with `pnpm backend:dev`, whose local verifier
# accepts any token, for end-to-end local play.
# NOTE: this test key returns the SAME dummy token every time, so it cannot serve as the
# backend's idempotency key — `backend:dev` knows that and keys each submission separately
# (see ScoreHandlerDeps.singleUseTokens). Production receives its real public key from the
# REQUIRED GitHub repo variable of the same name; vite.config.ts refuses a production build
# without it.
# THE PRODUCTION KEY MUST BE CREATED AS AN **INVISIBLE** WIDGET, not Cloudflare's default
# "Managed" one: a Managed key may escalate to an interactive challenge, and turnstile.ts
# renders into a hidden container with no way to show one. It would time out and silently
# drop the scores of exactly the players Cloudflare doubts. Nothing in code can check the
# widget type — this is a provisioning rule.
# Two other things to know when a local solved screen shows no standing: Vite
# reads this file at STARTUP (add the key, then restart
# `pnpm dev`), and a round that already submitted never re-submits — its persisted
# `scoreSubmitted` flag makes every later visit a read-only GET, so after restarting the
# backend (which clears its in-memory scores) clear the `whippin-round` localStorage key or
# play another day to get a fresh POST.
# That flag is also the RESIDUE of a REFUSAL, which is what a stuck local board usually is:
# any 4xx is a verdict the round never retries. `backend:dev` no longer caps submissions per
# address (it used to refuse the 6th identity of a day with a silent 429 — every local client
# shares 127.0.0.1), but a round already burned by one stays stuck until its flag is cleared,
# in the browser console:
#   const k='whippin-round', b=JSON.parse(localStorage[k]);
#   for (const m of [b.state.rounds, b.state.wordRounds]) for (const r of Object.values(m??{}))
#     { delete r.scoreSubmitted; delete r.scoreRecorded; }
#   localStorage[k]=JSON.stringify(b); location.reload();
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000BB
